</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.8 (build 660)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>A LIGHT pill in the header</b> marks a movie that is already light enough to play anywhere, where an optimized stand-in would say OPTIMIZED.</li>
<li><b>MXF is its own format.</b> MXF files are treated as camera footage: they default toward a camera log space rather than Rec.709, and the input space you choose for MXFs is remembered separately from other movies.</li>
<li>Optimized stand-ins of movies and image sequences that aren&#8217;t EXR now keep the original&#8217;s own color and follow its input space.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
